# Auth — sign in, refresh, and who am I.
#
# `/auth/login` is the only sign-in path. v1's `/auth/sign-in` is not aliased:
# v2.0.0 ships as a single cutover, so consumers move in the same release.
#
# Run "Sign in" first. Every other file that writes anything reuses this same
# pattern, because REST Client scopes a named request's response to the file it
# lives in: a token fetched in one .http file is not visible from another.
#
# Credentials come from the active environment (.vscode/settings.json), which
# reads them from your shell so no password is ever committed here.

@email = {{adminEmail}}
@password = {{adminPassword}}

### Sign in.
# @name login
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "{{email}}",
  "password": "{{password}}"
}

###

@accessToken = {{login.response.body.$.access_token}}
@refreshToken = {{login.response.body.$.refresh_token}}

### The signed-in user. The cheapest check that a token is good.
GET {{baseUrl}}/auth/profile
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### Trade a refresh token for a fresh pair.
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/refresh
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "refresh_token": "{{refreshToken}}"
}

# --- Failure cases. These are the ones worth re-running after touching auth. ---

### Wrong password -> 401 invalid_credentials.
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "{{email}}",
  "password": "definitely-not-the-password"
}

### Unknown email -> 401 invalid_credentials, with the same message and
# roughly the same timing as a wrong password. Different messages here would
# tell an attacker which addresses are real.
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "nobody@example.com",
  "password": "definitely-not-the-password"
}

### No token -> 401 missing_token.
GET {{baseUrl}}/auth/profile

### Malformed token -> 401 token_invalid.
GET {{baseUrl}}/auth/profile
Authorization: Bearer not.a.real.jwt

### An access token where a refresh token belongs -> 401 token_wrong_type.
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/refresh
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "refresh_token": "{{accessToken}}"
}

### v1's path is gone -> 404. Nothing should still be calling this.
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/sign-in
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "{{email}}",
  "password": "{{password}}"
}
